5,1,1,talk,Servas,,We must look at the past. I will examine the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts and the record of cross-unit standardization efforts.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Daisuke,,I’m worried about where the money actually comes from. I’ll check the capital budget and software allowance.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Sakura,,I’m curious about the real-world conditions! I’ll look into network coverage at customer plants and in-house developer availability.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,I will examine the time lost to copying existing records and the misrouted deliveries in the incident logs.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Asuka,,I will investigate the staffing of the coordination group and the handling of vendor queries.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Servas,,"@Daisuke, your caution is wise. Knowing the source of funds is the first step to understanding what we can truly afford.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Daisuke,,"Thank you, Servas. It’s just that the budget line is frozen, so I need to be sure what’s actually available before we commit.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, that’s smart! I’m checking if our developers are even free to build anything, so we don’t promise what we can’t deliver.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,I am focusing on the daily operational losses. We need to quantify the actual time wasted before judging any new tool.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Asuka,,"I am verifying who actually absorbs the workload. We cannot assume staff time is free, so I need to see the current coordination group staffing.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Servas,,"@Ryuji, quantifying daily losses is essential. We must ground our decisions in the reality of the floor, not just the promise of the pitch.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I agree. If the capital line is frozen, we must rely on the recurring allowance, which changes what is affordable.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Ryuji, I hope the logs show something interesting! I’m also checking if our developers are even free to build anything, so we don’t promise what we can’t deliver.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, if the developers are unavailable, the timeline is already broken. I need to know if the daily losses are worth that delay.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, the staffing gap is the real bottleneck. If the same two people are already drowning, adding another tool just breaks the rota faster.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
