35,2,1,talk,Servas,,#### Turn 1 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"- **Daisuke**: The capital line is frozen, but the recurring software allowance has room after those spring cancellations.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"- **Sakura**: Oh no! Half the customer plants lose signal all afternoon, and our developers are stuck until the third quarter.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,#### Turn 1 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: The coordination group is empty, yet two people still write every log by hand. Vendor queries are duplicated constantly.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,#### Turn 2 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"- **Daisuke**: That’s a relief. The recurring allowance is open, so we can fund something without touching the frozen capital line.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"- **Sakura**: @Daisuke, that’s good news! But with developers tied up and half the sites offline, how do we build anything that actually works?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,#### Turn 2 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Sakura, the staffing gap is the real bottleneck. If the same two people are already drowning, adding another tool just breaks the rota faster.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: @Daisuke, that recurring allowance is a lifeline. It means we can fund maintenance without touching the frozen capital, which is crucial.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"- **Daisuke**: Yes, it is. But I worry the real cost arrives with next year’s renewal notice, not today.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"- **Sakura**: @Asuka, that’s exactly my fear. If the groundwork is broken, no amount of funding fixes the missing hands.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, the duplicated vendor queries confirm the data is fragmented. I need to see if the daily copying losses match that pattern.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, the duplication is just the symptom. The real problem is that no one is left to fix it without breaking the current rota.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: I have reviewed the past. Tools needing daily entry from everyone were quietly dropped, while narrow, single-trade tools still run.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I’m relieved the recurring allowance is open. But I worry the real bill arrives with next year’s renewal notice, not today.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"- **Sakura**: @Servas, that explains why the narrow tools survived! We must avoid anything requiring daily entry from everyone.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"- **Ryuji**: The logs show eleven misrouted deliveries from duplicate addresses, and nearly an hour daily lost to copying. The data fragmentation is the root cause.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Ryuji, the data fragmentation is real, but the staffing gap is the immediate crisis. We cannot fix the data if no one is left to do the work.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
