60,3,1,talk,Servas,,"The candidates are A: Supplier Data Hub, B: Workflow Assistant, C: Training Studio, and D: Field Service App.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,- **Daisuke**: I see. Which of these fits within the recurring software allowance without triggering a large capital request?,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"- **Sakura**: @Daisuke, that’s the key! But @Servas, which of these actually works when half the sites have no signal?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,- **Ryuji**: The Supplier Data Hub directly targets the duplicate addresses causing our misrouted deliveries. It addresses the root cause I found.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"- **Asuka**: @Ryuji, the Hub requires constant updates. With the coordination group empty, who maintains it? We cannot add another burden to the drowning staff.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: @Asuka, you raise a valid point. Yet the past shows narrow tools survive. A central hub demands too much daily entry from everyone.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Servas, I agree. A hub demanding daily entry from everyone is exactly what gets quietly dropped. We need something narrower.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Servas, that makes sense! But @Ryuji, if the Hub is too broad, does the Field Service App work offline? I need to know if it survives the signal loss.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Servas"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, the app syncs records away from the network, so it handles the signal loss. But it still requires technicians to input data daily.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, daily input is precisely what kills these projects. If the coordination group is empty, who enforces the discipline?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: @Asuka, you are right. The Workflow Assistant drafts summaries, reducing the manual burden on those two drowning staff members.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Servas, that sounds helpful, but I worry about the recurring licence costs. Will it stay within the software allowance without a large capital request?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"- **Sakura**: @Daisuke, if it’s a fixed-fee build, the cost stays flat! But @Asuka, does it actually free up those two people, or just add another tool to manage?","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, it automates the summaries, saving the manual hours I measured. It reduces the daily copying burden without demanding new data entry.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, it reduces the writing, but it still requires someone to review and circulate the drafts. With the coordination group empty, that review burden remains.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Servas,,"- **Servas**: @Asuka, the review burden is real, but the past shows narrow tools survive. The Assistant is a single, focused aid, not a sprawling hub.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Servas, I agree. It fits the recurring allowance, unlike a capital project. But I worry the renewal notice will still arrive next year.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Sakura,,"- **Sakura**: @Daisuke, that’s a fair worry! But if it saves those two people hours daily, isn’t it worth the risk?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"- **Ryuji**: @Sakura, it saves the copying hours I measured. The daily loss is real, and this tool directly removes that specific burden.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, saving time is not the same as creating capacity. If the rota is already broken, automating the writing just leaves the review gap unfilled.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
